<interrogationes unitas="scriba_applicatio">

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I start the scriba editor as a standalone app with its own window or terminal?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_volumen_aperire scriba_applicatio_aedificare thema_initiare volumen_claudere" via="apps/scriba/scriba.c apps/scriba/scriba_terminalis.c">Call
      thema_initiare yourself (the glue owns the theme), open the
      volume with scriba_volumen_aperire(piscina, argc, argv, &amp;fumus),
      then scriba_applicatio_aedificare(&amp;app, piscina, intern, vol,
      latitudo, altitudo) with the surface size in our pixels. It
      builds the repository, mount, dispatcher and gesture slot; the
      main then only attaches its window or tty to app.d. Close the
      volume with volumen_claudere at exit.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what do -fumus and -volumen do on the scriba command line?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_volumen_aperire volumen_temporarium volumen_aperire_aut_creare">scriba_volumen_aperire
      scans argv: -fumus opens a temporary volume (volumen_temporarium
      with prefix scriba_fumus, deleted on volumen_claudere) and sets
      *fumus; -volumen PATH opens or creates that file; otherwise
      scriba.volumen in the current directory. Unknown arguments are
      ignored, and -volumen with no path after it is ignored too.
      NIHIL means the volume could not be opened.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I embed a scriba editor as one pane inside another app?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_montare scriba_montare_in_ramo ScribaMontatio" via="lib/vicus_applicatio.c lib/membrum__charta.c">Mount
      it into the host's InsulaRepositorium with scriba_montare(m, ...,
      repo, id, latitudo, altitudo, liber, systemata): id NIHIL uses
      the repository root, otherwise a child scriba element id is
      created under the root if absent. scriba_montare_in_ramo mounts
      under a parent branch instead (the calendar's day notes). Each
      mount has its own action and figura registries; its document is
      its own (in namespace id) when liber is NIHIL, else a page of the
      shared book chosen by the plagula scriba/visus/ID. systemata
      NIHIL means no persistence (tests).</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="possumne">
    <quaestio! (>can I copy a ScribaMontatio or ScribaApplicatio struct by value?
    <responsum symbolum="ScribaMontatio ScribaApplicatio scriba_montare">No.
      The action and figura contexts live INSIDE the ScribaMontatio and
      the registries point into them, so a copy leaves the registries
      pointing at the original. Keep the struct where you mounted it.
      ScribaApplicatio.doc, .actiones and .figurae are only aliases of
      the montatio fields.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="cur">
    <quaestio! (>why is my nested scriba mount refused when its id contains a hyphen?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_montare_in_ramo" via="lib/scriba_applicatio.worklog.md">The
      id becomes a canon nomen attribute on the branch, and the canon
      refuses '-' (write c1_notae, not c1-notae). The id also keys the
      page cursor plagula scriba/visus/ID and the saved state, so it
      must be unique in the whole volume. A NIHIL or empty id is
      refused with FALSUM.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quid">
    <quaestio! (>what size is the sheet of a newly created scriba document?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_montare scriba_documentum_creare">It
      follows the surface: the number of 6 x 8 cells in latitudo and
      altitudo minus one cell of margin on each side and, vertically,
      the status line, never less than 20 x 10. This applies only to a
      mount without a liber; an existing document, or a page of a
      book, keeps its own size. (The header's opening comment still says a
      new sheet is 68 x 56; that is no longer what the code does.)</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I keep two views of the same book in sync when one of them edits a page?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_reficere" via="lib/vicus_applicatio.c">Call
      scriba_reficere(m) on every pulse and BEFORE giving the view
      focus. It runs pending work and deferred commands, follows page
      navigation (m->doc catches up with the actions), refreshes the
      page indicator, and, when the document's cursor differs from the
      view's working cursor (another view committed), reloads the working sheet from the document. It returns VERUM
      when the pane must be repainted.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

  <interrogatio genus="quomodo">
    <quaestio! (>how do I switch a mounted scriba view to a different book without remounting?
    <responsum symbolum="scriba_librum_ponere insula_scriptorem_ponere" via="lib/membrum__charta.c">scriba_librum_ponere(m,
      liber) shows the page named by the view's plagula if it exists in
      the new book, else its first page; registries and contexts stay.
      The scriba branch's owners only admit the writer pagina.clavis,
      so it sets that writer for the call and restores the previous
      one. FALSUM if liber is NIHIL or the view was never
      mounted.</responsum>
  </interrogatio>

</interrogationes>
